---
layout: layouts/page.njk
title: Logo ideas
description: Six ways the laser burst logo from the old site could be worked into the Retro Garden theme.
eyebrow: logo-ideas.njk
section: design sandbox
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
<p>
  The old site used a laser burst mark in a blue-to-pink gradient, sitting to the left of
  the site name in the header. Below are six ways it could work in this theme. Each demo is
  live, so palette switching and hover states behave exactly as they would in production.
</p>

<h2>1. Header lockup</h2>
<p>
  Closest to the old site: the mark sits beside the wordmark. The beam points into the
  title, which gives the header a reading direction. This is the option I would ship first.
</p>
<div class="logo-demo">
  <a class="logo-lockup" href="#">
    {% include "components/site-logo.njk" %}
    <span class="logo-lockup__text">Sarah Kaiser</span>
  </a>
</div>

<h2>2. Fires on hover</h2>
<p>
  The beam is drawn on when you hover or focus the logo, so the laser appears to fire.
  It uses <code>stroke-dashoffset</code> and is disabled automatically under
  <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>.
</p>
<div class="logo-demo">
  <a class="logo-lockup logo-lockup--fires" href="#">
    {% set logoId = "fires" %}
    {% include "components/site-logo.njk" %}
    <span class="logo-lockup__text">Sarah Kaiser</span>
  </a>
  <p class="logo-demo__hint">Hover or tab to the logo above.</p>
</div>

<h2>3. Panel window chrome</h2>
<p>
  The mark shrinks into the title bar of a <code>retro-panel</code>, acting like an
  application icon in a window. Reinforces the desktop metaphor the theme already uses.
</p>
<div class="logo-demo">
  <div class="logo-window">
    <div class="logo-window__bar">
      {% set logoId = "chrome" %}
      {% include "components/site-logo.njk" %}
      <span>events.log</span>
    </div>
    <div class="logo-window__body">Panel content sits here.</div>
  </div>
</div>

<h2>4. Section divider</h2>
<p>
  A beam rule that replaces <code>pixel-divider</code> on bigger breaks, with the burst
  centred on the line. Good for separating major sections on long pages like About.
</p>
<div class="logo-demo">
  <div class="logo-rule" role="presentation">
    {% set logoId = "rule" %}
    {% include "components/site-logo.njk" %}
  </div>
</div>

<h2>5. 88&times;31 badge</h2>
<p>
  A proper old-web button in the existing badge wall, so the logo travels with link
  exchanges and webring-style footers.
</p>
<div class="logo-demo">
  <span class="logo-badge">
    {% set logoId = "badge" %}
    {% include "components/site-logo.njk" %}
    <span class="logo-badge__text">SCKAISER<br>.DEV</span>
  </span>
</div>

<h2>6. Favicon and social cards</h2>
<p>
  The same geometry works at 16&nbsp;px if the beam is dropped and only the burst is kept,
  and the full mark can be watermarked into generated OG images.
</p>
<div class="logo-demo logo-demo--row">
  <span class="logo-favicon" title="16px favicon treatment">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 140 140" role="img" aria-label="Favicon treatment">
      <defs>
        <linearGradient id="logo-favicon-gradient" x1="15" y1="70" x2="125" y2="70" gradientUnits="userSpaceOnUse">
          <stop offset="0" stop-color="var(--logo-start, #80d8ff)" />
          <stop offset="1" stop-color="var(--logo-end, #ea80fc)" />
        </linearGradient>
      </defs>
      <g fill="none" stroke="url(#logo-favicon-gradient)" stroke-width="16" stroke-linecap="round">
        <path d="M15 70 H125" />
        <path d="M70 15 V125" />
        <path d="M31 31 L109 109" />
        <path d="M109 31 L31 109" />
      </g>
    </svg>
  </span>
  <div class="logo-og">
    {% set logoId = "og" %}
    {% include "components/site-logo.njk" %}
    <div class="logo-og__text">
      <p class="eyebrow">sckaiser.dev</p>
      <p class="logo-og__title">Quantum computing, open source, and community</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
